<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Find the coefficient of <m>x^{2}</m> in the expansion of <m>{\left(2-3x\right)^{6}}</m>. Give a number, not a term.</p><div><fillin characters="8" name="ans1"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>The term in <m>x^{2}</m> takes number <m>{2}</m> of the row for power <m>{6}</m> (counting from 0), the first term to the power <m>{4}</m> and the second term to the power <m>{2}</m>. It is the 3rd term.</p><p>Number <m>{2}</m> of the row for power <m>{6}</m> is <m>{15}</m>. The term is</p><p><me>{15} \times {2}^{4} \times \left({-3 x}\right)^{2} = {15} \times {16} \times {9}x^{2} = {2160 x^2}</me></p><p>so the coefficient of <m>x^{2}</m> is <m>{2160}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>2160</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>